#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0719 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a BDS dataset contains none of the subject-level or record-level treatment variables defined in the IG.
#note "Only trt01a is present — spelled in lower case as a SAS dataset may carry it; column names match case-insensitively on every surface (owner ruling 2026-09-28), templates included. It is a member of the TRTxxA family defined in the IG (ADaMIG 1.1/1.2/1.3 Table 3.2.4 (ADSL treatment variables, any of which may be copied into a BDS dataset)), so the CR719 requirement is met: the Check's count(find_vars('TRTxxA')) == 0 term is false, the rule runs and passes (PLAN-dynamic-column-corpus-respelling phase 2 — the template moved from Requirements.Variables.None into the Check, the AD0581 shape of R-5.31; this dataset used to be SKIPPED, which misreported a conformant dataset as 'could not check')."
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL type=Num
col trt01a type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 12.5 | X
---
